Subject: [PATCH 24/25] docs: validate the merged image by building it, and fix
 a third probe defect
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The kit previously said, three times over, that the image had never been built
and that the Dockerfile reproducing the run was an argument rather than a
measurement. It is now a measurement.

Built on BOTH cluster nodes from this branch's source (not built once and
shipped -- the claim under test is that the Dockerfile reproduces the run), then
G0-G2 and both stress gates re-run against it with NO in-container patching.
Every gate matched the patched-image run, including the two numbers that
discriminate: kvd 102 gets / 102 hits with sets UNCHANGED after an engine
restart, and the router's prefill view at 51 blocks under MTP.

Adds scripts/verify_built_image.sh -- 18 bytecode/source assertions plus a
behavioural smoke test. A build log saying a patch printed success is not the
same as the interpreter running patched code; a stale .pyc has already
invalidated a full experiment here.

Two expected differences from the patched image, both recorded rather than
smoothed over: the two nodes' image ids DIFFER (independent builds, so Rust
objects and layer timestamps differ -- check content equivalence, not digests),
and the built image carries ONE infera copy instead of two, so the shadowing
trap in notes.md §3 cannot arise there.

The third probe defect (notes.md §6c), which cost the most time:

  All four probes sent `temperature: 0`. GLM-5.2's own generation_config.json
  says temperature 1.0, top_p 0.95. Greedy decoding sends a reasoning model into
  repetition on a long prompt and EAGLE/MTP AMPLIFIES it -- the draft model
  predicts the loop perfectly, so `accept len` pins at its maximum and the
  response runs to max_tokens. G2 read 3/5 with the needle missing, </think> x
  1264, and depth 1.0 the only clean one, which is EXACTLY the early-send
  signature. The fix was in the bytecode and correctly wired the whole time.

  Settled by control rather than by argument: MTP off, same image, same prefill
  leg, same prompt -> 5/5. MTP back on with the official sampling -> 5/5, accept
  len back to 2.17-2.60. The same defect inflated conc=128 to 5/256 BAD, all of
  them at the output cap; raising OSL alone dropped it to 1/256, matching the
  validated run.

  needle.py and stress_capture.py now send the model's own values. probe.py and
  prefix_reuse.py are left greedy on purpose -- at 64 and 128 max tokens they
  cannot reach the degenerate regime.

Also corrects a claim the raw JSON never supported: the stress table said
"0 corrupt" at conc=128, while results/raw/stress_c128.json has 1
CORRUPT_REASONING. Both images show exactly 1/256, in both cases the single
response that ran to the cap, and in both cases a plain repetition loop with
</think> x 0 -- not the chunk-boundary signature, which requires the tag to
cycle. Replaying that prompt at conc=1 returns CLEAN.

